# API Integration Rules

## Constants
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL` — define only in `.env.local` (local) or the host's env (production). Read via `getPublicApiBaseUrl()` from `src/lib/env.ts` — never read `process.env` ad hoc in components.
- Never put secrets in `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` variables (they ship to the browser).
- All API path segments → `src/lib/constants/api.ts` (`API_ENDPOINTS`).

## Services (`src/lib/services/`)
- One file per feature: `auth.ts`, `home.ts`, `horoscope.ts`, `panchang.ts`, etc.
- Each function is typed: accepts typed params, returns typed response (from `src/types/`).
- Use `axios` instance configured in `src/lib/services/http.ts` (base URL + interceptors).
- Wrap calls in try/catch and throw a typed `ApiError` for consumers to handle.

## Hooks (`src/hooks/`)
- Name: `use<Feature>.ts` — e.g. `useAuth.ts`, `useDashboard.ts`.
- Always expose `{ data, isLoading, error }` shape.
- Never call `fetch` or `axios` directly inside a component — go through a hook.
- Use `zustand` stores for global client state (auth session, user profile).

## Auth
- Auth token stored via `zustand` + `localStorage` (mirrors Flutter LocallySavedData).
- Attach token in `src/lib/services/http.ts` request interceptor.
- On 401 response, clear token and redirect to `/login`.
